Z||000000||kiss||07-06-2001||10:24 PM||||OK! IM NEW TO THE FORUM. I DRIVE A 88 GT AND I WANT TO DROP THE CAR. IN THE REAR THE FIERO STORE DROP SPRINGS ARE FINE. BUT IN THE FRONT IT IS NOT ENOUGH. NOBODY MAKES A SPRING TO LOWER IT MORE THAN 3/4 INCH. MAYBE THE SUSPENSION IS NOT BUILT TO SAFELY HANDLE MORE THAN A 3/4 DROP. SO EVERYBODY RECOMMENDS HELD (RAYNE). 2739 MEMBERS 90,000 POSTS, AND YET I'VE NOT READ THAT ANYONE HAS THEM. ARE THEY REALLY THE BEST? THEY ARE SO EXPENSIVE! WHO HAS THEM? WHO HAS TESTED THEM?<BR>I'VE HAD MY FIERO SINCE 1995 AND NEVER RAN INTO ANYONE THAT HAS HAD THESE DROP SPINDLES. SO WHAT OTHER CHOICES ARE THERE REALLY? SO I ASK " WHY HELD"? EVERYBODY WANTS TO BUY THEM, BUT BODY HAS THEM!<BR>THANX<BR>A FRUSTRATED 88 ||||reg||1
