Z||000003||chester||07-07-2001||09:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kiss:<BR><B>OK! IM NEW TO THE FORUM. I DRIVE A 88 GT AND I WANT TO DROP THE CAR. IN THE REAR THE FIERO STORE DROP SPRINGS ARE FINE. BUT IN THE FRONT IT IS NOT ENOUGH. NOBODY MAKES A SPRING TO LOWER IT MORE THAN 3/4 INCH. MAYBE THE SUSPENSION IS NOT BUILT TO SAFELY HANDLE MORE THAN A 3/4 DROP. SO EVERYBODY RECOMMENDS HELD (RAYNE). 2739 MEMBERS 90,000 POSTS, AND YET I'VE NOT READ THAT ANYONE HAS THEM. ARE THEY REALLY THE BEST? THEY ARE SO EXPENSIVE! WHO HAS THEM? WHO HAS TESTED THEM?<BR>I'VE HAD MY FIERO SINCE 1995 AND NEVER RAN INTO ANYONE THAT HAS HAD THESE DROP SPINDLES. SO WHAT OTHER CHOICES ARE THERE REALLY? SO I ASK " WHY HELD"? EVERYBODY WANTS TO BUY THEM, BUT BODY HAS THEM!<BR>THANX<BR>A FRUSTRATED 88 </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I can say that I feel your pain! Fortunatly for me I was dealing with an 86 GT and not an 88. Unfortunatly, you are limited on the selection when it comes to the 88 suspension. Actually your limited when it comes to the Fiero period. There is no doubt in my mind that drop spindles ARE THE WAY TO GO! I have a set from street dreams but once again they only make them for 84-87 models. If you want the drop and you want to do it right - PAY THE MAN!  I had a modified setup that I purchased second hand that someone fabricated a 2" drop into the suspension by means of their own and the suspension failed on me while I was 450 miles away from home. Not a fun time. Upper control arm ripped off the cross member. Glad it happened in the gas station parking lot and not on the interstate at 80MPH! Anyway enough rambling from me. I saw the spindles in person at the Carlisle show. Well made. The reason that not many have them is two fold. Not many mess with their 88 suspension because it was nice from the factory. Second is, like you mentioned, the cost. But hell, its like anything else - YOU GET WHAT YOU PAY FOR! <P>Later<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
